Chapter: Minimax
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Games chapter TicTacToe
  cites Games chapter Connect4

 Iterative minimax search for bare-metal environments with limited stack.
 Instead of recursive calls that blow the stack, each search is performed
 with a flat loop: try every legal move, apply it, then for each response
 try every legal counter-move and evaluate statically. This gives effective
 depth-2 (two-ply) lookahead with call depth that never exceeds two
 function calls. Scores are integers: positive favors player 1, negative
 favors player 2.

 We say:

Section: Types

  MmConfig = record {
    max-depth  : Integer,
    eval-fn-id : Integer
  }

  MoveScore = record {
    move  : Integer,
    score : Integer
  }

Section: TicTacToe Iterative AI

 Score a finished or evaluated TicTacToe position from player 1's
 perspective. Win for 1 = +100, win for 2 = -100, draw or ongoing = 0.

  ttt-static-score : TttBoard -> Integer
  ttt-static-score (b) =
    if b.game-over then
      if b.winner == 1 then 100
      else if b.winner == 2 then -100
      else 0
    else 0

 Count empty squares remaining on the board.

  ttt-empty-count : TttBoard, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ttt-empty-count (b) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 9 then acc
    else if ttt-empty b i then ttt-empty-count b (i + 1) (acc + 1)
    else ttt-empty-count b (i + 1) acc

 Evaluate depth-1 response: given a board after our move, let the opponent
 try every legal reply and return the worst-case score for the maximizing
 player (player 1). Opponent minimizes.

  ttt-min-response : TttBoard, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ttt-min-response (b) (col) (worst) =
    if col >= 9 then worst
    else if b.game-over then worst
    else if ttt-empty b col == False then ttt-min-response b (col + 1) worst
    else let after = ttt-move b col
    in let s = ttt-static-score after
    in let next-worst = if s < worst then s else worst
    in ttt-min-response b (col + 1) next-worst

 Evaluate depth-1 response for maximizer (player 1 choosing best reply).

  ttt-max-response : TttBoard, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ttt-max-response (b) (col) (best) =
    if col >= 9 then best
    else if b.game-over then best
    else if ttt-empty b col == False then ttt-max-response b (col + 1) best
    else let after = ttt-move b col
    in let s = ttt-static-score after
    in let next-best = if s > best then s else best
    in ttt-max-response b (col + 1) next-best

 Score a single candidate move for the current player. After applying the
 move, if the game is over we return the static score immediately. Otherwise
 we let the opponent search their best reply (depth-1 lookahead) and return
 that. The current player is determined by b.current-player before the move.

  ttt-score-move : TttBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ttt-score-move (b) (pos) =
    let after = ttt-move b pos
    in if after.game-over then ttt-static-score after
    else if b.current-player == 1 then ttt-min-response after 0 100
    else ttt-max-response after 0 (-100)

 Search all nine squares, track the best move and score for the current
 player. Returns the best column index found.

  ttt-best-move : TttBoard, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ttt-best-move (b) (col) (best-col) (best-score) =
    if col >= 9 then best-col
    else if b.game-over then best-col
    else if ttt-empty b col == False then ttt-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score
    else let s = ttt-score-move b col
    in if b.current-player == 1 then
      if s > best-score then ttt-best-move b (col + 1) col s
      else ttt-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score
    else
      if s < best-score then ttt-best-move b (col + 1) col s
      else ttt-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score

 Public entry point: return the best move index (0-8) for the board's
 current player using two-ply iterative search.

  ttt-iterative-ai : TttBoard -> Integer
  ttt-iterative-ai (b) =
    if b.game-over then -1
    else let init-score = if b.current-player == 1 then -101 else 101
    in ttt-best-move b 0 (-1) init-score

Section: Connect4 Iterative AI

 Static heuristic for Connect4 from player 1's perspective.
 Win = ±1000. Otherwise use center-column preference as tiebreaker.

  c4-static-score : Connect4Board -> Integer
  c4-static-score (b) =
    if b.game-over then
      if b.winner == 1 then 1000
      else if b.winner == 2 then -1000
      else 0
    else c4-positional-score b

 Sum a positional bonus across all filled cells. Center columns score
 higher for player 1, lower for player 2.

  c4-positional-score : Connect4Board -> Integer
  c4-positional-score (b) =
    c4-pos-loop (b.squares) 0 0

  c4-pos-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  c4-pos-loop (sq) (idx) (acc) =
    if idx >= 42 then acc
    else let col = idx - (idx / 7) * 7
    in let bonus = c4-col-bonus col
    in let piece = list-at sq idx
    in let delta = if piece == 1 then bonus
                   else if piece == 2 then -bonus
                   else 0
    in c4-pos-loop sq (idx + 1) (acc + delta)

  c4-col-bonus : Integer -> Integer
  c4-col-bonus (col) =
    if col == 3 then 4
    else if col == 2 then 2
    else if col == 4 then 2
    else if col == 1 then 1
    else if col == 5 then 1
    else 0

 Depth-1 minimizing response: opponent picks worst-for-us reply.

  c4-min-response : Connect4Board, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  c4-min-response (b) (col) (worst) =
    if col >= 7 then worst
    else if b.game-over then worst
    else if c4-col-full b col then c4-min-response b (col + 1) worst
    else let after = connect4-drop b col
    in let s = c4-static-score after
    in let next-worst = if s < worst then s else worst
    in c4-min-response b (col + 1) next-worst

 Depth-1 maximizing response: player 1 picks best reply.

  c4-max-response : Connect4Board, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  c4-max-response (b) (col) (best) =
    if col >= 7 then best
    else if b.game-over then best
    else if c4-col-full b col then c4-max-response b (col + 1) best
    else let after = connect4-drop b col
    in let s = c4-static-score after
    in let next-best = if s > best then s else best
    in c4-max-response b (col + 1) next-best

 Score a single candidate column drop. Two-ply: apply move, then let
 opponent pick their best one-ply reply.

  c4-score-move : Connect4Board, Integer -> Integer
  c4-score-move (b) (col) =
    let after = connect4-drop b col
    in if after.game-over then c4-static-score after
    else if b.current-player == 1 then c4-min-response after 0 1001
    else c4-max-response after 0 (-1001)

 Scan all seven columns, return the best column for current player.

  c4-best-move : Connect4Board, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  c4-best-move (b) (col) (best-col) (best-score) =
    if col >= 7 then if best-col >= 0 then best-col else 3
    else if b.game-over then if best-col >= 0 then best-col else 3
    else if c4-col-full b col then c4-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score
    else let s = c4-score-move b col
    in if b.current-player == 1 then
      if s > best-score then c4-best-move b (col + 1) col s
      else c4-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score
    else
      if s < best-score then c4-best-move b (col + 1) col s
      else c4-best-move b (col + 1) best-col best-score

 Public entry point: return the best column (0-6) for the current player
 using two-ply iterative search.

  c4-iterative-ai : Connect4Board -> Integer
  c4-iterative-ai (b) =
    if b.game-over then -1
    else let init-score = if b.current-player == 1 then -1002 else 1002
    in c4-best-move b 0 (-1) init-score

